      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CLANG AND BANG (7) showed good early speed and led throughout to score his maiden two back then finished fourth last start and beaten 6 lengths at this track over 300m (17.41). Returns to the scene of his maiden win. Key player on best and worth another chance. GRANDPA JOE (1) doesn't have the best strike-rate. Better run when finding the frame last time though, finishing third (20.18) at Grafton. Has never missed the frame from four starts from this draw, including a win. Expected to be in the finish again. DODGEM MOCHA (4) skirted wide from an outside draw last start and found the front, leading throughout to win (23.53) at this track in a Maiden over 411m. Must be included in calculations. BIG WEST (2) gets a chance to improve on an unplaced run at his latest outing at this circuit.",
